# b12x notes. NO BASE_SHA256 here, deliberately: nothing upstream is replaced or
# hooked. This directory installs a third-party package (b12x, Apache-2.0,
# https://pypi.org/project/b12x/) into the container by mounting it, and vLLM's
# own b12x code -- already in the image -- takes it from there.
#
# Mechanism (Plan 06):
#   ./fetch            downloads the wheel pinned in b12x.env, checks its sha256,
#                      unpacks it to $CACHE_DIR/b12x/<version>/site (a wheel is a zip;
#                      the image has no pip and needs none).
#   zz_b12x.pth        one line, /opt/b12x-site. Mounted into the venv's site-packages,
#                      it APPENDS that directory to sys.path, so a b12x the image itself
#                      ships (a later Dockerfile line) wins and this overlay goes inert.
#   b12x_args          common/_run-lib.sh: mounts site/ :ro at /opt/b12x-site plus the
#                      .pth when MOE_BACKEND or NVFP4_BACKEND is exactly "b12x"
#                      (B12X=1 forces, B12X=0 refuses).
#
# What vLLM imports from it (vllm/utils/b12x.py, _B12X_SUBMODULES @ 4d9a8d6):
#   b12x.attention.paged, b12x.gemm.blockscaled, b12x._lib.intrinsics (private!),
#   b12x.gemm.mxfp8_linear, b12x.gemm.tensor_fp8_linear, b12x.moe.fused_moe
# A missing submodule degrades to "not supported" for that kernel, and an explicit
# --moe-backend b12x / --linear-backend b12x then fails at engine init with vLLM's
# own message rather than silently picking something else.
#
# Dependencies it declares (requires_dist) -- all already in the g4d9a8d6 image:
#   torch>=2.12 (2.14.0), cuda-python (13.4.4), nvidia-cutlass-dsl and its four
#   -libs-* ==4.8.0 (4.8.0), apache-tvm-ffi >=0.1.6,<0.2, !=0.1.8 (0.1.11),
#   rich>=13 (15.0.0), transformers>=4.51 (5.19.0), safetensors>=0.6 (0.8.0).
# Re-check them on every repin: vLLM pins b12x exactly (setup.py "b12x" extra), and a
# torch or cutlass-dsl move in the image can break it with no change here.
#
# JIT cache: CuTe-DSL compiles go to $XDG_CACHE_HOME / ~/.cache, i.e. the launcher's
# rw $CACHE_DIR mount -- a warm boot reuses them.
#
# Confirmed 2026-10-16 on iphands/vllm-blackwell:cu1321-sm120-main-vllm0.33.0.dev20261015-g4d9a8d6,
# --gpus device=0: all six submodules import; B12xMxfp8LinearKernel, B12xNvFp4LinearKernel,
# B12xFp8BlockScaledMMKernel, B12xTensorFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel is_supported() == (True, None);
# B12xExperts._supports_current_device() == True.
#
# fe8f214 repin (2026-10-18): THE IMAGE NOW SHIPS b12x ITSELF, and this overlay goes
# inert there, as designed above. vllm#61913 takes flashinfer-python to 0.7.2. Its
# wheel embeds b12x 1.5.0 under flashinfer.experimental.b12x and installs a top-level
# compat package, `b12x` (flashinfer#5767; pyproject.toml package-dir
# "b12x" = "flashinfer/experimental/b12x/_compat/b12x"). Our flashinfer-build builds
# that same pyproject. The package sits in site-packages and our .pth only appends,
# so `import b12x` resolves to flashinfer's embedded copy, not the mounted 1.5.1.
# All six vLLM submodules above exist in the embedded tree at flashinfer v0.7.2.
# vLLM's extra still pins b12x==1.5.1 (setup.py:1732). Flashinfer's copy
# is 1.5.0 plus its own fixes, among them flashinfer#6294 (skip unrouted -1 routes
# in the W4A16 top-k sum), #6317 (W4A16 E8M0 re-bias) and #6211 (SM12x direct-micro
# input scale, static-kernel recompiles).
# Disposition: retired-kept. It still does its job for IMAGE_TAG=<the g4d9a8d6 tag>.
# On the fe8f214 image it mounts but cannot win, and b12x_args still prints
# "1.5.1 mounted", which would then be false. Whether to drop the mount for images
# that ship b12x, or make the .pth prepend so the pinned wheel wins, is a Plan 06
# decision. Neither is made here. NOT VERIFIED until the image is built: that our
# flashinfer wheel actually carries the top-level b12x package.
# Decided 2026-10-18 (Plan 06 T5, owner): DROP the mount on images that ship b12x.
# b12x_args reads the image's ai.vllmcustom.flashinfer.version label (`image inspect
# --format`, metadata only) and, at >= 0.7.2 (B12X_IMAGE_SINCE_FLASHINFER), mounts
# nothing and skips the not-fetched refusal under B12X=auto. B12X=1 still mounts, with
# an "inert" warning, as the escape hatch if the label ever lies about an image. A
# missing or unparsable label keeps the old mount-and-refuse path. The label is a
# proxy for "the wheel carries b12x". The first boot of a fe8f214 image settles it:
# a b12x backend either selects (`Using 'B12X' NvFp4 MoE backend`) or fails at
# engine init with vLLM's own unsupported message.
